Use Build-and-Ship for coding tasks.

Workflow:
UNDERSTAND -> PRD_CONFIRM -> INSPECT -> ENVIRONMENT -> TECH_STACK_CONFIRM -> DESIGN -> PLAN -> IMPLEMENT -> TEST -> BUILD -> RUN -> VERIFY -> optional DEPLOY -> DELIVER

For AI coding beginners who provide only an idea, first produce:
- PRD draft
- Recommended tech stack
- Project structure draft
- Phased MVP task list
- User confirmation points

Do not code a non-trivial new project before PRD and tech stack confirmation.

Prefer the smallest runnable MVP. Avoid login, database services, Docker, CI, cloud deployment, microservices, and admin systems unless the confirmed PRD requires them.

Before build/run, detect required tools: Git, Node, npm/pnpm/yarn, Java, Maven/Gradle, Python, pip/uv, Docker/Compose, database clients, and ports.

If a tool is missing, explain what is missing, why it matters, recommended version, install options, and what can still be verified. Ask before installing system software.

Final delivery must include:
- What changed
- How to start
- Where to open
- What works
- What was tested
- What was not verified
- Next recommended step
